# Reference scenario "intro-no-card": title screen -> New Game -> no memory card -> continue without
# saving -> 3D introduction (first dialogue, which waits for A). Converts the old scenario in .txt format
# (seconds of emulated time -> presented frames; the START press at 50 s, which had no effect on the title screen, is removed).
# Format: tools/scenario.py (times in PRESENTED FRAMES, numbered from 1; no game data here).
# Written on GGTP01 with the last build that still emulated the hardware (kept outside this repository's public
# history; cycle clock, RTC 800000000); its reference run is now recorded natively (tools/ab.py record). The checkpoints are on screens
# that wait for an input, except "loading" (simulated disc read time: soft, never makes the comparator fail).
name intro-no-card
description Title screen, New Game, no memory card, continue without saving, 3D intro.
version GGTP01
window 4
env GCRT_CARD=absent   # empty port A: this scenario follows the "no memory card" path (as the emulated build did)

input  150 A       # 60/50 Hz prompt: confirm the 50 Hz option
input 1050 A       # health and safety warning
input 2600 A       # title screen: New Game
input 2900 A       # no-memory-card message: A goes on without saving
input 3100 LEFT    # prompt to confirm playing without saving: cursor from No (preselected) to Yes
input 3250 A       # confirm Yes -> loading, clock scene, birthday party

check  800 health-warning
check 2000 title-screen
check 2800 no-card
check 3060 continue-without-saving
check 3200 yes-selected
check 3330 loading soft
check 4000 birthday-dialogue

end 4150
